# Terraform
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Terraform state can contain secrets in plain text (never commit it!). Your
# state lives on your own machine for this homework; in a real team it would
# live in a shared remote backend (S3 + DynamoDB, Terraform Cloud, Pulumi
# Cloud) so everyone plans against the same reality.

# Build artifacts (Part 2's deployment package)
build/
*.zip

# Pulumi
# `pulumi login --local` keeps state under ~/.pulumi, but `pulumi login file://.`
# puts it right here and Pulumi state is every bit as sensitive as Terraform's.
.pulumi/
node_modules/
bin/
Pulumi.*.yaml.bak

# Local overrides
*.auto.tfvars
terraform.tfvars

.DS_Store
